<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!-- ============================================================================
         SCRUM-107: PAI NO LONGER MINTS ITS READ SOURCES, AND THAT IS AN ORDERING
         CONTRACT.

         000-bootstrap.xml is deleted. It bootstrap-created three relations PAI does
         not own, in unguarded raw-SQL blocks, so that PAI could run on a fresh
         database before their owners ever had:

           tx_header, tx_entry ...... PRR owns them (R-04 single writer)
           account .................. nobody in this family owns it; the acs service
                                      is being built to own it, in dcre_acs

         A reader minting the writer's schema is the shared-table coupling the family
         split exists to remove, and it is not merely untidy. PRR's baseline creates
         tx_header and tx_entry UNGUARDED, so a PAI mint that won the race would make
         PRR crashloop on "relation already exists". The mint was also a hand-copied
         mirror that nothing compared against the owner, which is a drift class: PAI's
         suite would stay green against a column set PRR had already changed. This is
         the same retirement collections/crg performed, copied rather than reinvented.

         THE CONTRACT: PAI's migration must run AFTER PRR's. On a fresh dcre_pay, PAI
         migrating first now fails loudly and immediately, naming the missing relation
         instead of inventing a wrong one. That is the correct failure.

         THE OPEN EDGE, recorded rather than left to be discovered: nothing creates
         account in dcre_pay at all, because nothing should. AccountRepo still issues
         INSERT INTO account against the primary datasource, so PAI cannot complete a
         run against a real dcre_pay until acs ships and AccountRepo is repointed at
         the acs datasource. That repointing is owned elsewhere and is deliberately
         NOT worked around here with a mint, because a mint is what put PAI's schema
         in the wrong database in the first place. Integration tests stand all three
         relations up from src/test/resources/db/changelog/test/001-read-sources.xml.
         ============================================================================ -->

    <include file="db/changelog/2026/07/001-pai.xml"/>
    <include file="db/changelog/2026/07/002-batch-metadata.xml"/>

</databaseChangeLog>
